uence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "callout": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "formula": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "table": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "code": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "compare": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "grid": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "flow": "create-diagram: Author structural diagram, graph, flow, and timeline blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use graph for explicit named edges, branching, hierarchy, or convergence; diagram when a fixed shape carries the relationship; flow for one simple linear chain; timeline only for events with explicit times or stages. Use state-sim when understanding depends on intermediate states or transformations rather than a fixed relationship. Affordances: spatial-structure, node-edge-relations, hierarchy, sequence, chronology. Learner actions: inspect, trace, compare. Evidence outputs: named-relations, fixed-structure, linear-sequence, chronology. Limitations: fixed-state-only, no-coordinate-proof, no-hidden-transition.", "timeline": "create-diagram: Author structural diagram, graph, flow, and timeline blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use graph for explicit named edges, branching, hierarchy, or convergence; diagram when a fixed shape carries the relationship; flow for one simple linear chain; timeline only for events with explicit times or stages. Use state-sim when understanding depends on intermediate states or transformations rather than a fixed relationship. Affordances: spatial-structure, node-edge-relations, hierarchy, sequence, chronology. Learner actions: inspect, trace, compare. Evidence outputs: named-relations, fixed-structure, linear-sequence, chronology. Limitations: fixed-state-only, no-coordinate-proof, no-hidden-transition.", "diagram": "create-diagram: Author structural diagram, graph, flow, and timeline blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use graph for explicit named edges, branching, hierarchy, or convergence; diagram when a fixed shape carries the relationship; flow for one simple linear chain; timeline only for events with explicit times or stages. Use state-sim when understanding depends on intermediate states or transformations rather than a fixed relationship. Affordances: spatial-structure, node-edge-relations, hierarchy, sequence, chronology. Learner actions: inspect, trace, compare. Evidence outputs: named-relations, fixed-structure, linear-sequence, chronology. Limitations: fixed-state-only, no-coordinate-proof, no-hidden-transition.", "graph": "create-diagram: Author structural diagram, graph, flow, and timeline blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use graph for explicit named edges, branching, hierarchy, or convergence; diagram when a fixed shape carries the relationship; flow for one simple linear chain; timeline only for events with explicit times or stages. Use state-sim when understanding depends on intermediate states or transformations rather than a fixed relationship. Affordances: spatial-structure, node-edge-relations, hierarchy, sequence, chronology. Learner actions: inspect, trace, compare. Evidence outputs: named-relations, fixed-structure, linear-sequence, chronology. Limitations: fixed-state-only, no-coordinate-proof, no-hidden-transition.", "freeform": "create-freeform: Author a freeform block for a LectureDoc lecture — the long-tail fallback for a visual relationship that none of the formal block types can express, drawn as inline SVG/HTML restricted to theme colour tokens. Reach for it only after checking the structured types: graph covers trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts; chart covers data; diagram covers fixed shapes; grid and sim.widget cover custom layouts and interactive pieces. When it genuinely is the right tool it now renders as normal page content, so use it without hedging.", "geometry-sim": "create-geometry-sim: Plan a spatial constraint simulation for a LectureDoc lecture. Use when coordinate mapping, dragging, boundaries, vectors, geometric construction, or spatial invariants are themselves the learning evidence. Do not use merely because a state diagram has positioned nodes; AVL rotations remain state-sim. The final block lowers to sim.widget. Affordances: drag, coordinate-map, constraint, construction, spatial-transform. Learner actions: manipulate, construct, predict, inspect. Evidence outputs: coordinate-change, constraint-preservation, spatial-invariant. Limitations: not-decorative-layout, not-discrete-structure, not-code-execution.", "stats": "create-infographic: Author stats blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use only to spotlight 2-6 standalone key numbers whose individual magnitude is the evidence; use chart for trends, distributions, or correlations and create-diagram for structural relationships. Affordances: standalone-metrics, fixed-state. Learner actions: inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: key-number. Limitations: no-trends, no-structural-relations, no-unsourced-numbers.", "model-sim": "create-model-sim: Plan a parameterized model simulation for a LectureDoc lecture. Use when learners must change real parameters and observe a recomputed quantitative consequence, compare model regimes, or inspect deterministic or stochastic causal behavior. Use chart for a fixed dataset and state-sim for discrete algorithm steps. Lowers to the shared sim runtime. Affordances: parameter-control, recompute, comparison, stochastic, history. Learner actions: manipulate, predict, calculate, compare. Evidence outputs: parameter-output-map, regime-change, quantitative-cause. Limitations: not-fixed-dataset, not-code-execution, not-discrete-structure.", "quiz": "create-quiz: Author a quiz block for a LectureDoc lecture — objective (multiple-choice, auto-graded) or subjective (open discussion prompt). Reach for it whenever a page should check understanding or provoke reflection rather than only present — at least one per lecture is encouraged. Objective for a checkable fact/skill, subjective for open-ended thinking. Affordances: elicited-response, auto-grading, misconception-diagnosis. Learner actions: predict, calculate, judge, explain. Evidence outputs: student-answer, correctness-feedback, explanation. Limitations: one assessment chain per block.", "state-sim": "create-state-sim: Plan a discrete state simulation for a LectureDoc lecture. Use whenever learning evidence depends on an algorithm's intermediate states, stepwise execution, tree/graph/array mutation, structural transformation, replay, or before-to-after mapping. AVL rotations and data-structure updates belong here even though nodes have positions. The final block lowers to sim.widget. Affordances: state-transition, step, reset, playback, history, comparison. Learner actions: trace, predict, manipulate, construct. Evidence outputs: intermediate-state, transition-sequence, before-after-map. Limitations: not-static-snapshot, not-code-execution, not-coordinate-constraint."}, "currentBrief": {"objective": "学生能描述 AVL 树插入算法的步骤：递归插入、更新高度、检查平衡、旋转调整", "learningAction": "trace", "requiredEvidence": "学生能对给定插入序列，逐步画出树的变化", "keyClaim": "AVL 树插入通过递归实现，每次插入后从插入点向上回溯，更新高度并检查平衡因子，必要时旋转", "misconception": "插入后只检查插入点的父节点", "visualTask": "展示多步插入过程中，每个节点的高度和平衡因子变化，以及旋转发生的位置", "evidencePolicy": "provided"}, "currentScene": {"id": "insert-algorithm", "kind": "content", "headline": "插入算法：递归插入 + 回溯调整", "lead": "插入 5,6,3,4,1,2 到空树，观察每一步的递归回溯与旋转。", "notes": "用一个多步插入例子展示完整的插入算法流程", "blocks": [{"type": "sim", "engine": "widget", "html": "<style>
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .root { width:100%; height:100%; min-width:0; min-height:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; font-family:var(--font-sans, system-ui, sans-serif); background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink); }
  .ctrl-row { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; padding:8px 12px; flex-shrink:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
  .ctrl-row button { padding:6px 16px; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg2); color:var(--ink); font-size:13px; cursor:pointer; transition:background .12s, transform .12s; }
  .ctrl-row button:hover { background:var(--accent); color:var(--bg); }
  .ctrl-row button:active { transform:scale(.97); }
  .ctrl-row .step-label { font-size:13px; color:var(--text2); margin-left:auto; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  .stage { flex:1; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; min-height:0; padding:8px; }
  .stage svg { width:100%; height:100%; max-height:420px; display:block; }
  .readout { display:flex; gap:16px; padding:6px 12px; border-top:1px solid var(--line); font-size:12px; color:var(--text2); flex-shrink:0; flex-wrap:wrap; }
  .readout span { white-space:nowrap; }
  .readout .hl { color:var(--accent); font-weight:500; }
  .node-circle { transition:fill .2s, stroke .2s; }
  .node-text { font-size:13px; font-weight:500; font-family:var(--font-mono, monospace); }
  .bf-text { font-size:11px; font-family:var(--font-mono, monospace); }
  .edge-line { stroke:var(--line); stroke-width:1.5; }
</style>
<div class="root">
  <div class="ctrl-row">
    <button id="prevBtn" disabled>← 上一步</button>
    <button id="nextBtn">下一步 →</button>
    <button id="resetBtn">重置</button>
    <span class="step-label" id="stepLabel">步骤 0 / 6</span>
  </div>
  <div class="stage" id="stage">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 600 360" id="treeSvg"></svg>
  </div>
  <div class="readout" id="readout">
    <span>插入序列: <span class="hl">5, 6, 3, 4, 1, 2</span></span>
    <span id="actionMsg">空树</span>
  </div>
</div>
<script>
  (function(){
    const svg = document.getElementById('treeSvg');
    const stage = document.getElementById('stage');
    const stepLabel = document.getElementById('stepLabel');
    const actionMsg = document.getElementById('actionMsg');
    const prevBtn = document.getElementById('prevBtn');
    const nextBtn = document.getElementById('nextBtn');
    const resetBtn = document.getElementById('resetBtn');

    // ---------- math_model: AVL tree states ----------
    // Each state: { nodes: [{id, val, x, y, bf, highlight, rotateAxis}], edges: [{from, to}] }
    function buildStates() {
      const states = [];
      // step 0: empty
      states.push({ nodes: [], edges: [], action: '空树' });
      // step 1: insert 5
      states.push({
        nodes: [{id:0, val:5, x:300, y:60, bf:0, highlight:'new', rotateAxis:false}],
        edges: [],
        action: '插入 5，根节点'
      });
      // step 2: insert 6
      states.push({
        nodes: [
          {id:0, val:5, x:300, y:60, bf:-1, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:1, val:6, x:420, y:160, bf:0, highlight:'new', rotateAxis:false}
        ],
        edges: [{from:0, to:1}],
        action: '插入 6，节点 5 BF=-1'
      });
      // step 3: insert 3
      states.push({
        nodes: [
          {id:0, val:5, x:300, y:60, bf:0, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:1, val:6, x:420, y:160, bf:0, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:2, val:3, x:180, y:160, bf:0, highlight:'new', rotateAxis:false}
        ],
        edges: [{from:0, to:1}, {from:0, to:2}],
        action: '插入 3，节点 5 BF=0'
      });
      // step 4: insert 4
      states.push({
        nodes: [
          {id:0, val:5, x:300, y:60, bf:-1, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:1, val:6, x:420, y:160, bf:0, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:2, val:3, x:180, y:160, bf:-1, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:3, val:4, x:240, y:260, bf:0, highlight:'new', rotateAxis:false}
        ],
        edges: [{from:0, to:1}, {from:0, to:2}, {from:2, to:3}],
        action: '插入 4，节点 3 BF=-1，节点 5 BF=-1'
      });
      // step 5: insert 1
      states.push({
        nodes: [
          {id:0, val:5, x:300, y:60, bf:-1, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:1, val:6, x:420, y:160, bf:0, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:2, val:3, x:180, y:160, bf:0, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:3, val:4, x:240, y:260, bf:0, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:4, val:1, x:120, y:260, bf:0, highlight:'new', rotateAxis:false}
        ],
        edges: [{from:0, to:1}, {from:0, to:2}, {from:2, to:3}, {from:2, to:4}],
        action: '插入 1，节点 3 BF=0，节点 5 BF=-1'
      });
      // step 6: insert 2 → LR rotation
      states.push({
        nodes: [
          {id:0, val:4, x:300, y:60, bf:0, highlight:'', rotateAxis:true},
          {id:1, val:6, x:420, y:160, bf:0, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:2, val:3, x:180, y:160, bf:0, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:3, val:5, x:360, y:160, bf:0, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:4, val:1, x:120, y:260, bf:0, highlight:'', rotateAxis:false},
          {id:5, val:2, x:240, y:260, bf:0, highlight:'new', rotateAxis:false}
        ],
        edges: [{from:0, to:1}, {from:0, to:2}, {from:1, to:3}, {from:2, to:4}, {from:2, to:5}],
        action: '插入 2 → LR 旋转，树平衡'
      });
      return states;
    }
    const states = buildStates();

    // verification
    (function verify(){
      console.assert(states.length === 7, 'should have 7 states');
      console.assert(states[0].nodes.length === 0, 'step0 empty');
      console.assert(states[1].nodes.length === 1 && states[1].nodes[0].val === 5, 'step1 root 5');
      console.assert(states[6].nodes.length === 6, 'step6 6 nodes');
      console.assert(states[6].nodes[0].val === 4, 'step6 root 4 after rotation');
    })();

    // ---------- render ----------
    let step = 0;

    function update() {
      const s = states[step];
      // clear
      svg.innerHTML = '';
      // edges
      s.edges.forEach(e => {
        const fromNode = s.nodes.find(n => n.id === e.from);
        const toNode = s.nodes.find(n => n.id === e.to);
        if (!fromNode || !toNode) return;
        const line = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'line');
        line.setAttribute('x1', fromNode.x);
        line.setAttribute('y1', fromNode.y + 20);
        line.setAttribute('x2', toNode.x);
        line.setAttribute('y2', toNode.y - 20);
        line.setAttribute('class', 'edge-line');
        svg.appendChild(line);
      });
      // nodes
      s.nodes.forEach(n => {
        const g = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'g');
        const circle = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'circle');
        circle.setAttribute('cx', n.x);
        circle.setAttribute('cy', n.y);
        circle.setAttribute('r', 20);
        circle.setAttribute('class', 'node-circle');
        let fill = 'var(--bg2)';
        let stroke = 'var(--line)';
        let strokeWidth = 1.5;
        if (n.highlight === 'new') {
          fill = 'var(--accent)';
          stroke = 'var(--accent)';
          strokeWidth = 2.5;
        }
        if (n.rotateAxis) {
          stroke = 'var(--accent)';
          strokeWidth = 3;
        }
        circle.setAttribute('fill', fill);
        circle.setAttribute('stroke', stroke);
        circle.setAttribute('stroke-width', strokeWidth);
        g.appendChild(circle);
        // value text
        const text = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'text');
        text.setAttribute('x', n.x);
        text.setAttribute('y', n.y + 4);
        text.setAttribute('text-anchor', 'middle');
        text.setAttribute('class', 'node-text');
        text.setAttribute('fill', n.highlight === 'new' ? 'var(--bg)' : 'var(--ink)');
        text.textContent = n.val;
        g.appendChild(text);
        // bf label
        const bfText = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'text');
        bfText.setAttribute('x', n.x + 26);
        bfText.setAttribute('y', n.y - 6);
        bfText.setAttribute('class', 'bf-text');
        bfText.setAttribute('fill', n.bf === 2 || n.bf === -2 ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--text2)');
        bfText.textContent = 'BF=' + n.bf;
        g.appendChild(bfText);
        svg.appendChild(g);
      });
      // step label
      stepLabel.textContent = `步骤 ${step} / 6`;
      actionMsg.textContent = s.action;
      prevBtn.disabled = step === 0;
      nextBtn.disabled = step === 6;
    }

    // ---------- interactions ----------
    function goStep(delta) {
      const newStep = step + delta;
      if (newStep < 0 || newStep > 6) return;
      step = newStep;
      update();
    }
    function reset() { step = 0; update(); }

    nextBtn.addEventListener('click', () => goStep(1));
    prevBtn.addEventListener('click', () => goStep(-1));
    resetBtn.addEventListener('click', reset);

    // initial paint
    update();
  })();
